Z||000000||Bill H||10-22-2000||02:34 PM||||  I own a 88 formula and it is time for more power. Do any of you have a Fiero that runs 1/4 mile times in the 13s? I'm wondering who much power this will take.  thanks Bill||||reg||1
Z||000001||HYPTNOTiSE||10-22-2000||03:47 PM||||A v-8 conversion would be the easiest way to achieve 13's. I say that sadly but true.  My fiero v-6 engine and transmission has been modified/built, and i expect 13 second second times on the motor with the setup, and hope to see 12's with nitrous.  Although my setup doesn't include, AC, cruise control, and A lot of weight elimination has been done. The car is very stiff, i have all solid motor mounts, and a very non streetable clutch going in. I have about 4-5K dollars in my 3.2 liter 6 cyl.  think about how much HP i could have made with a 383cid chevy with that much money. I could be going 11's. My engine's cam profile is setup for nitrous/supercharger.  Nitrous is on now, and supers comming later. I want 12's all day long.  <P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||10-22-2000||03:48 PM||||At least 250 HP<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||10-22-2000||04:58 PM||||yep, 250-300 hp sound rite. But its lots more fun to race someone on a twisty country road. Even stock power on those makes Fiero fly. Let someone try to catch you in their badddd 'Stang or Camaro.||||reg||1
