Z||000011||BBBAD GT||10-23-2000||01:22 PM||||Roger:  No offense taken.  I just like pointing out to people that the dragstrip doesn't have any turns when the discussion gets off topic.<P>Thats exactly why I bought a Fiero, great handling.  Where else are you going to get a true mid engine feel for so little dollar?  I'll leave the strip to the Mustang.  I've been kidding myself thinking the Mustang could be a handler also.  Although the suspension isn't bad for cone chasing (I've tried that a couple time, can you say steer with your right foot?), the motor just wants to scream.  Sorry for the rambling.....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fieroboy1||10-23-2000||09:02 PM||||Easiest way to get a fiero into the 13's is to drop it off a 1/4 mile cliff....lol.  All kidding aside my Uncle owns probably the quickest fiero in the us unless one of you guys knows of a fiero quicker than 10.26. And unfortunately he didn't have all the power to the ground for that timeslip. The car is an 86 SE it was on Archie's website for a while.  500 hp small block.  Believe it was a zz3 or bow tie block.  Brodix heads and i believe 13:1 compression.  The kicker was the 250 hp big shot nitrous.  The car uses a custom beefed fiero automatic since the car liquified the isuzu 5 speed.  The car actually ripped the motor mounts through the cradle.  It's been sitting for a while since my uncle is playing with his race ready Vega.  The fiero is for sale if anyone is interested. I believe he wants somewhere in the neighborhood of 10,000.<BR>Sorry for the rant<BR>John<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Greg Piet||10-24-2000||03:48 PM||||FieroBoy...  I might know a "Fiero" (I must use the word loosely) that will beat it.  It is called a "Fiero Tomcat" by the owner...  it kind of looks like a Fiero, but the only stock Fiero parts I can see are the taillights and the shifter...  Its a tubeframe and it is a 500hp+ V8 in it... IT IS TRULY AN ANIMAL!<P>Not to try to outdo you or your uncle, but the car in describing is insane.<P>He races the car on road courses, so obviously it handles like it si on rails but I believe there was a grudge match between him and someone else, and I thought he ran in the 9's on the 1/4, but I am NOT SURE... Please dont get defensive or angry, just sharing some info.<BR>Peace man Peace!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fieroboy1||10-24-2000||05:21 PM||||Yeah man, that's why i mentioned it, just curious to see if anyone has a better timeslip.  The 86 se i described is STOCK BODIED with only a few weight reductions like removing the headlights and the gas tank in favor of a 4 gallon racing cell.  The car also has a rollcage and recaro racing seat.  But the car is a transverse v/8 archie kit, and like i said it was on archie's website forever; listed under Pat ciarcia's ultimate nhra fiero.  ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Dan86gt3.8||10-24-2000||08:46 PM||||Well the quickest way I know with no nos is to do a 3.8 sc with a getrag.  I believe forum member "robertvol" ran a 13.6 with his and he did not push it all the way.  That and   I bet a semi hoped up lt1 or about a 300hp v8 would do the trick quite nice.<P>ohhh and guys there are a couple of pro stock  fieros with the engines in front that are running 10's. check out <A HREF="http://www.boomtastic.com" TARGET=_blank>www.boomtastic.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
